[list]
[*]Shift Change no longer walks through every other mod's buttons when it has nothing of its own to add. Its change-back button is appended to the list of buttons RimWorld builds for each selected colonist, and that list is rebuilt every frame; the old version enumerated the whole list, other mods' buttons included, before deciding whether to add anything at all. It now checks the colonist first and steps aside when they are not wearing a stand's outfit, which is nearly always.
[*]You will not notice this, and it would be dishonest to suggest otherwise. The work removed comes to a few microseconds per frame even with a full squad selected, far below anything you could see. It is worth fixing because it sat on a path the game runs constantly while doing nothing there for most colonists, not because it was costing anyone frames.
[*]The same change applies to the "Allow removing items" toggle on stands that Shift Change does not govern. A stand you have set to "Not used for shift changes" is now left alone entirely, rather than inspected every time it is selected.
[*]Nothing about how stands behave has changed. The change-back button appears exactly when it did before, including while the safety latch that stops automatic changing has tripped, and the toggle is still held off on stands that are in service. Three new cases in the release gate cover both, so a future cleanup cannot quietly undo it.
[/list]
